# Scoping rule for THIS directory: derived and extracted artifacts stay out.
#
# TbFence 4.00 is 1990s shareware licensed by ESaSS B.V. (Thunderbyte is the
# brand, not the licensor). Its own LICENSE.DOC does permit mirroring:
# "The evaluation package of the TbFence software may be distributed freely
# without charge in evaluation form only", provided the package is complete and
# unaltered — which is the case for retro-dos/tbfence4.zip, and why the
# originals are kept there rather than deleted.
#
# What must NOT be committed here is everything *this* directory generates:
# extracted binaries, Ghidra projects, analysis output. Those are neither the
# complete package nor unaltered, so the licence's carve-out does not cover
# them. Full per-archive terms: ../../retro-dos/NOTICE.md (REPO-2).
_src/
analysis/
*.exe
*.com
*.sys
*.dat
*.zip
